    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **39 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + householdId`, rejecting with 409 only on an exact whole-key match.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **New `OwnerIdentityKey.of(Owner)`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 the one place the key is derived: telephone normalized to E.164, email trimmed/lower-cased, householdId as-is (empty segments when absent). Used both for the check and the response so they can't drift.\n- **New `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** step \u2014 compares the new owner's full key against every existing owner's; throws the new checked `OwnerIdentityConflictException` (\u2192 409 via `OwnerIdentityConflictExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML). Wired into `owners.POST.yml` **after** `assignHousehold` (so `householdId` is part of the key) and before `save` (so the not-yet-saved owner isn't compared to itself).\n- **Removed** the three separate checks (`CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, `CheckOwnerEmailUnique`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`) and their exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs; `validate` now flows straight to `checkCityCapacity`.\n- **`identityKey` returned** \u2014 added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (readOnly) and populated by an `OwnerMapper` expression, so it appears on both create and GET responses.\n\n**Behaviour delivered**\n\n- A full duplicate (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28) or same last-name+address+telephone household (Cp10) now collides via the single key \u2192 409.\n- Because telephone is in the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`, different telephones) have distinct keys and are both allowed (Cp11), which also confirms the exact `telephone||householdId` format for an empty email.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: this is a deliberate behaviour change \u2014 previously, a second owner reusing an existing telephone (or email) with *different* other fields was rejected; now it's only rejected when the entire `telephone|email|householdId` key matches. That is exactly what the spec and the updated tests require.",
